.\" blink(1) -- the Blink command-line tool.
.\" Keep in step with docs/CLI.md and usage() in tools/blink.c;
.\" tests/python/test_harness.py checks that every option is in all three.
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
.Dd September 22, 2026
.Dt BLINK 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm blink
.Nd score one typed decision with a Blink model
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar model.blink
.Fl -state Ar text
.Op Fl -question Ar text
.Fl -option Ar text
.Fl -option Ar text
.Op Fl -option Ar text ...
.Op Fl -no-verify
.Nm
.Ar model.blink
.Fl -info
.Op Fl -no-verify
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
answers one question of the form
.Dq given this state and this criterion, which of these options?
It opens a
.Pa .blink
container, encodes the state, the question and every option in a single
forward pass, and prints one probability per option as one line of JSON.
There is no text generation: the options are the only possible answers.
.Pp
The probabilities are conditional on the options given and sum to one.
Text is read as raw bytes, so any encoding works.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -state Ar text
The unstructured state to decide about: a ticket, a log line, a JSON
document.
Required for a decision.
It may be empty only when a question is given, because a decision needs at
least one byte of context.
.It Fl -question Ar text
The criterion, chosen at call time.
Optional; empty by default.
.It Fl -option Ar text
One declared option.
Give it at least twice and at most 32 times; options are scored in the order
given.
An option must not be empty.
.It Fl -no-verify
Skip the CRC-32 check of the container when opening it.
.It Fl -info
Print the model's geometry as JSON and exit, without scoring anything.
.It Fl -version
Print the library version and the numeric backend it runs on this CPU, as in
.Dl blink 0.1.0 (neon)
and exit.
The backend is one of
.Cm scalar , neon , sse2 , avx2 , accelerate ,
or, for a W8A8 build,
.Cm w8a8-scalar , w8a8-sdot , w8a8-i8mm , w8a8-sse2 , w8a8-avx2 .
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print a usage summary on standard output and exit.
.El
.Pp
Each of state, question and option has a byte limit set by the model,
reported by
.Fl -info
as
.Cm max_state ,
.Cm max_question
and
.Cm max_option .
Longer input is refused, not truncated.
.Sh OUTPUT
A decision prints one JSON object:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm options
One object per option, in the order given, with its
.Cm text
and its
.Cm probability .
.It Cm argmax
The index of the most probable option, counting from zero.
.It Cm confidence
The probability of that option.
.It Cm margin
Its probability minus the runner-up's.
.It Cm entropy
The entropy of the distribution, in nats.
.It Cm context_positions
Pooled positions of state and question the options attended over.
.It Cm encode_seconds , Cm head_seconds
Time spent encoding and in the option head.
.El
.Pp
.Fl -info
prints the model's
.Cm name ,
its geometry
.Pq Cm width , blocks , ffn_width , rank , heads , conv_width , stride , bigram_buckets ,
its byte limits
.Pq Cm max_state , max_question , max_option ,
the calibration
.Cm temperature ,
.Cm parameters ,
.Cm weights_bytes
and the
.Cm session_arena_bytes
a session with 16 options needs.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev BLINK_X86_SIMD
On x86-64,
.Cm scalar , sse2
or
.Cm avx2
forces that kernel instead of the one chosen for the CPU.
.It Ev BLINK_W8A8_KERNEL
In a W8A8 build,
.Cm scalar , sdot , i8mm , sse2
or
.Cm avx2
forces that integer kernel.
A kernel the CPU or the build lacks is ignored.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
Success.
.It 1
The model could not be opened, a session could not be created, or the
decision failed: input over the model's limits, an empty option, or no
context at all.
The reason is printed on standard error.
.It 2
A usage error: a missing or unknown argument, fewer than two options or more
than 32.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Route a support ticket:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
blink blink-tiny.blink \e
  --state "The parcel left the depot on Monday and has not arrived." \e
  --question "Which team should handle this ticket?" \e
  --option "delivery and logistics" \e
  --option "billing and payments" \e
  --option "account access and sign-in"
.Ed
.Pp
Take the answer in a shell script, escalating when the model is unsure:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
blink model.blink --state "$ticket" --option refund --option replace |
  jq -r 'if .confidence < 0.8 then "escalate"
         else .options[.argmax].text end'
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
The C API in
.Pa blink.h ,
and
.Pa docs/CLI.md
in the Blink repository,
.Lk https://github.com/sqliteai/blink .
For many rows at once, use
.Pa eval/evaluate.py ,
which drives the same library and reuses a cached state.
